{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe journey from Brussels to Ghent was uneventful, save for the heat in the diligence. I spent the afternoon in Ghent viewing the Ghent Altarpiece panels. Van Eyck’s light is uncanny; it feels less like paint and more like a window into a different epoch. I arrived in Bruges by canal barge at 8 p.m. The cabin was cramped, filled with men playing whist with a fervor that bordered on the religious. I watched a hand for an hour; one player’s arrogance was positively comical, though his play was sound.\n\nDinner was adequate, if uninspiring. I paid three francs for a modest meal and a bottle of local wine. I am tired, and the barge rocked enough to unsettle my stomach. I think of you and the boys here in the quiet of this Flemish town. The air is damp. I hope Karl is studying diligently and Immanuel is not causing trouble. I shall write again when I reach Paris.\n\nYours always,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219415,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":223,"prompt_tokens":1112,"total_tokens":1335,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Deb9PJlxc8Vy9OkyuJw4yJtiaTgGhCDv","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1112,"prompt_ms":1040.569,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9357634892086331,"prompt_per_second":1068.6460965106592,"predicted_n":223,"predicted_ms":5169.838,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.28755855855856,"predicted_per_second":42.94138423679814}}